==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ang|sƿīcan||wynn spelling}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*swīkwan}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*swīkwaną}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*swem(bʰ)-|t=to bend, turn, swing}}.<ref>{{R:ine:IEW|3030}}</ref>

Cognate with {{cog|ofs|swīka||stay far from}}, {{cog|osx|swīkan||betray, languish}}, {{cog|dum|swiken}} ({{cog|nl|bezwijken||give way, sink}}), {{cog|goh|swīhhan}} (dialectal {{cog|de|schweichen||wander round, deceive}}), {{cog|non|svíkva||betray}} ({{cog|sv|svika}}, {{cog|da|svige}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|swīcan}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|swīcan}}

# to wander, to move about
# to [[deceive]], be treacherous

